payload.core_explanation_md:
**Policy** spells out: **tolerance, funding strategy, prudential limits, measuring and reporting system, stress testing framework, contingency plan, reporting frequency, review of assumptions**; also covers **currencies, legal entities, business lines** and **limits on transfers of liquidity**.

**Tolerance** (**set by the Board**): the **level of liquidity risk the bank will assume**, reflecting **financial condition and funding capacity**, so it can **survive prolonged bank-specific and market-wide stress**. It can be set as:
- **maturity-wise mismatch levels** (flow approach), keeping **mismatches up to 30 days at minimum levels**;
- **limits on stock ratios**;
- **minimum survival horizons** under **severe but plausible stress**.

**Strategy** must **fit the nature, scale and complexity** of the bank and **name primary funding sources for daily outflows**. **Identification** covers **each on and off-balance sheet position, embedded options and contingent exposures, in every currency**.

